---
import summary from '../../../benchmarks/results/summary.json'
import { tasks } from '../../../benchmarks/tasks.mjs'
import CodeBlock from './CodeBlock.astro'

interface Row {
  version?: string
  runs: number
  launchMs?: number
  snapshotMs?: number
  snapshotTokens: number
  fullSnapshotTokens: number
  screenshotMs?: number
  tasksPassed: number
  tasksRun: number
  retries?: number
  taskMs?: number
  taskTokens: number
  perSite: Record<
    string,
    {
      snapshotMs?: number
      snapshotTokens?: number
      fullSnapshotTokens?: number
      screenshotMs?: number
      loadMs?: number
    }
  >
  perTask: Record<
    string,
    { passed: number; runs: number; ms?: number; tokens?: number; errors: string[] }
  >
}
const tools = summary.tools as Record<string, Row>
const names = Object.keys(tools)
const env = summary.environment as Record<string, string | number | undefined>
const repo = 'https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/benchmarks'
const show = (value?: number) =>
  value === undefined ? '–' : Math.round(value).toLocaleString('en-US')
const seconds = (value?: number) => (value === undefined ? '–' : `${(value / 1000).toFixed(1)} s`)
// The best value in a column, so it can be marked.
const best = (key: keyof Row, lower = true) => {
  const values = names
    .map((name) => tools[name]?.[key])
    .filter((value): value is number => typeof value === 'number')
  return lower ? Math.min(...values) : Math.max(...values)
}
const mark = (key: keyof Row, value: unknown, lower = true) =>
  value === best(key, lower) ? 'accent' : ''
const hosts = Object.keys(tools[names[0] ?? '']?.perSite ?? {})
const command = 'node benchmarks/run.mjs --rounds 3'
// Every column suitecut does not win, worded from the data, so the page never hides one.
const columns: [keyof Row, string, string][] = [
  ['launchMs', 'Launch', 'ms'],
  ['snapshotMs', 'Snapshot', 'ms'],
  ['snapshotTokens', 'Snapshot tokens', 'tokens'],
  ['screenshotMs', 'Screenshot', 'ms'],
  ['taskMs', 'Task time', 'ms'],
  ['taskTokens', 'Task tokens', 'tokens'],
]
const ours = tools.suitecut
const behind = columns.flatMap(([key, label, unit]) => {
  const value = ours?.[key]
  if (typeof value !== 'number') return []
  const leader = names.find((name) => name !== 'suitecut' && tools[name]?.[key] === best(key))
  // browser-use reads only the viewport and 1000 px around it, not the whole page.
  const partial =
    leader === 'browser-use' && unit === 'tokens'
      ? ' (browser-use reads only around the viewport)'
      : ''
  return leader
    ? [`${label}: ${leader} ${show(best(key))} ${unit}, suitecut ${show(value)} ${unit}${partial}`]
    : []
})
---

<h2 id="agents">suitecut, agent-browser and browser-use</h2>
<p>
  The same {hosts.length} public pages and {tasks.length} read-only tasks, three of them across several
  pages, run by each tool from a cold start. Every script and every raw result is in
  <a href={repo}>benchmarks/</a>, and the whole run is one command.
</p>
<p class="muted">
  {String(env.date).slice(0, 10)} · {env.cpu} · {env.memoryGB} GB · {env.os} · suitecut {
    env.suitecut
  }
  ({env.commit}) · agent-browser {env.agentBrowser} · browser-use {env.browserUse} on {env.chrome} · {
    summary.rounds
  }
  rounds per tool
</p>

<div class="table-scroll">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Tool</th>
        <th>Launch</th>
        <th>Snapshot</th>
        <th>Snapshot tokens, {hosts.length} pages</th>
        <th>Screenshot</th>
        <th>Tasks passed</th>
        <th>Task time</th>
        <th>Task tokens, {tasks.length} tasks</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {
        names.map((name) => {
          const row = tools[name]!
          return (
            <tr>
              <td>{name}</td>
              <td class={mark('launchMs', row.launchMs)}>{show(row.launchMs)} ms</td>
              <td class={mark('snapshotMs', row.snapshotMs)}>{show(row.snapshotMs)} ms</td>
              <td class={mark('snapshotTokens', row.snapshotTokens)}>{show(row.snapshotTokens)}</td>
              <td class={mark('screenshotMs', row.screenshotMs)}>{show(row.screenshotMs)} ms</td>
              <td class={mark('tasksPassed', row.tasksPassed, false)}>
                {row.tasksPassed}/{row.tasksRun}
                {row.retries ? <span class="muted"> · {row.retries} retried</span> : null}
              </td>
              <td class={mark('taskMs', row.taskMs)}>{seconds(row.taskMs)}</td>
              <td class={mark('taskTokens', row.taskTokens)}>{show(row.taskTokens)}</td>
            </tr>
          )
        })
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="muted">
  Medians. Bold is the best in each column. Tokens are characters ÷ 4 of the text an agent reads.
</p>
{
  behind.length > 0 && (
    <>
      <h3>Where suitecut is behind</h3>
      <ul>
        {behind.map((line) => (
          <li>{line}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </>
  )
}

<h3>Tasks</h3>
<div class="table-scroll">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Task</th>
        {names.map((name) => <th>{name}</th>)}
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {
        tasks.map((task) => (
          <tr>
            <td>
              {task.goal}
              <br />
              <span class="muted">
                <code>{task.name}</code>
              </span>
            </td>
            {names.map((name) => {
              const row = tools[name]?.perTask[task.name]
              return (
                <td>
                  {row ? `${row.passed}/${row.runs}` : '–'}
                  <br />
                  <span class="muted">
                    {seconds(row?.ms)} · {show(row?.tokens)} tokens
                  </span>
                </td>
              )
            })}
          </tr>
        ))
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h3>Pages</h3>
<div class="table-scroll">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Page</th>
        {names.map((name) => <th>{name}</th>)}
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {
        hosts.map((host) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{host}</td>
            {names.map((name) => {
              const row = tools[name]?.perSite[host]
              return (
                <td>
                  {show(row?.snapshotTokens)} tokens
                  <br />
                  <span class="muted">
                    snapshot {show(row?.snapshotMs)} ms · screenshot {show(row?.screenshotMs)} ms
                  </span>
                </td>
              )
            })}
          </tr>
        ))
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h3>How it is measured</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    Each round starts every tool with a new browser and an empty profile, headless at 1280×720 and a
    scale factor of 1. The tool order rotates each round.
  </li>
  <li>
    Each page is loaded to its <code>load</code> event and left for 1.5 s, then snapshotted and screenshotted
    3 times each; the tables use the median call.
  </li>
  <li>
    The snapshot is the text each tool gives an agent: suitecut
    <code>ariaSnapshot(&#123; mode: 'ai', interactive: true &#125;)</code>, agent-browser
    <code>snapshot -i</code> (the mode its documentation recommends) and browser-use
    <code>llm_representation()</code>. browser-use leaves out elements more than 1000 px outside the
    viewport, so its snapshot does not cover the whole page.
  </li>
  <li>
    A task reads a snapshot before each step and acts on the first element whose role and name
    match, using the tool's own ref. Each action may take 5 s; one that fails gets a new snapshot
    and one more try, as an agent would, and is counted as retried. A task passes when the URL
    reaches the goal within 20 s. There is no LLM: the same choices are made for every tool, so only
    the browser layer is measured.
  </li>
  <li>
    browser-use runs with its extensions off (one hides cookie banners), so every tool loads the
    same page. agent-browser times include starting its CLI per command, as an agent calls it.
  </li>
  <li>
    These are live sites over a home connection on a working machine; network time and load vary.
    The raw <a href={`${repo}/results/results.json`}>results.json</a> keeps every call and the load average
    of each round.
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>Run it yourself</h3>
<CodeBlock label="Terminal" code={command} />
<p>
  <a href={`${repo}/README.md`}>benchmarks/README.md</a> has the setup for each tool. The pieces:
  <a href={`${repo}/run.mjs`}>run.mjs</a>, <a href={`${repo}/tasks.mjs`}>tasks.mjs</a>,
  <a href={`${repo}/adapters/suitecut.mjs`}>suitecut</a>,
  <a href={`${repo}/adapters/agent-browser.mjs`}>agent-browser</a> and
  <a href={`${repo}/adapters/browser_use.py`}>browser-use</a> adapters, and
  <a href={`${repo}/report.mjs`}>report.mjs</a>. What changed in suitecut is in the
  <a href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">changelog</a>.
</p>

<style>
  td.accent {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
